# 0. Executive result

SoloRing still has one dominant reusable-production dependency spine, but the revised graph shows more clearly that several high-value branches can advance independently.

The dominant authority spine is:

```text
minimal publishable Production Revision
        ↓
Composition Revision
        ↓
stable addressable Production Instance
        ↓
identity preservation across Composition Revision evolution
        ↓
instance-bound world-state + spatial integration
        ↓
Composition ↔ Spatial binding
        ↓
coherent Shot production-context capture
        ↓
historical reusable-production closure
        ↓
production-world observation support
```

Two completeness thresholds remain load-bearing:

```text
AUTHORITY-COMPLETE REUSABLE WORLD
SoloRing can remember the exact reusable world, occurrences, state, spatial bindings,
and historical Shot usage without consulting current mutable state.

RENDERABLE REUSABLE WORLD
That captured world can additionally be compiled into executor-facing observations,
with hard preservation requirements rejected before queueing when unsupported.
```

The revised graph also proves four important independence statements:

- entity-bound intra-Shot consequences do not depend on the reusable-production spine;
- the generalized observation contract can be designed from existing specialized compilation foundations before new production-world inputs exist;
- basic QC can evaluate Takes against existing captured authority before the generalized trust vocabulary exists;
- camera-only candidate-world adoption can target existing spatial/cinematic authority without solving reusable object identity first.

Deferred universal rigging, simulation, candidate-world ingestion, broad Sound Post, editorial, collaboration, and continuous-story-clock work remain outside the reusable-world spine. Dialogue/vocal performance is no longer classified as broad Sound Post: it is an A1/A7 prerequisite of production-grade lip sync.

