### v1.2-preserved publication refinement

The first publishable Production Revision requires **enough retained representation identity/bytes and interpretation metadata to satisfy its declared consumption closure**. It does not require the full generalized `RP-02` multi-representation registry first.

This keeps the first publication slice narrow while preserving APR-081:

```text
Production Revision identity
    ≠
any one representation
```

`RP-02` remains required when the product needs first-class multiple consumer representations, selection, replacement, compatibility, or representation-specific lifecycle.

