# 8. Dependency cut points

## 8.1 RP-03 — first publishable reusable revision

Before `RP-03`, SoloRing may retain candidate/working content but lacks an immutable consumption-closed reusable production revision suitable for Composition or historical capture.

`RP-03` no longer means “the generalized representation registry is complete.” It means the first declared downstream use can consume the exact retained revision deterministically.

## 8.2 CO-02 — durable occurrence identity

Before `CO-02`, the production cannot reliably say:

> This is the exact same Chair 7 occurrence later in the film.

## 8.3 CO-03 — occurrence continuity across publication

Before `CO-03`, persistent state or spatial continuity attached to an occurrence is unsafe under Composition Revision evolution.

## 8.4 BD-01 — exact composition/spatial agreement

Before `BD-01`, Composition and spatial authority may each be internally valid while disagreeing about occurrence↔subject mapping or realization interpretation.

## 8.5 SH-02 — resolved stateful reusable-world Shot

Before `SH-02`, the current world may be coherent but its Production/Composition/Instance/state/spatial combination is not yet immutable Shot history.

## 8.6 HI-01 — historical reusable-production closure

Before `HI-01`, new reusable-world identities can be captured without proving retained closure and current-state independence.

## 8.7 OB-02 — renderable production world

Before `OB-02`, SoloRing can remember/capture the reusable world but has not yet proven that the new reusable-production facts constrain final execution through the generalized observation path.

---


## 8.8 ED-02 — authoritative editorial decision boundary

Before `ED-02`, SoloRing may have approved source Takes and exact media inspection, but it cannot yet say which exact source intervals, order, and editorial placements constitute an authoritative edit independent of proxy or executor syntax.

