# 12. Dependency risks

## 12.1 Overbuilding reusable-production representation

Do not turn `RP-02` into a speculative universal asset/representation framework before a real Composition/observation consumer proves the need. The first source gate should prove `RP-01/RP-03` consumption closure for one real downstream path.

## 12.2 Treating Composition as a scene-file wrapper

Occurrence identity must live in SoloRing authority, not only inside one representation hierarchy or namespace.

## 12.3 Duplicating spatial authority in Composition

`BD-01` maps authority-bound occurrences to A4 spatial truth. It does not grant Composition a competing placement authority.

## 12.4 Hiding binding compatibility inside CM-01

`BD-01` must state its own required interpretation facts. A future compatibility service may supply reusable evidence, but binding correctness cannot depend on an undefined monolithic compatibility engine.

## 12.5 Delaying historical closure until renderer work

`HI-01` must close before `OB-02` can claim historical production-world observation. Otherwise reusable production becomes a current-state convenience layer.

## 12.6 Calling a wrapper a generalized observation compiler

`OB-01` can be designed early; `OB-02` is the proof that new Production/Composition/Instance state actually reaches execution.

## 12.7 Requiring generalized trust semantics before useful QC

Basic QC should exploit existing captured authority now. The future trust vocabulary should enrich it, not delay it.

## 12.8 Reversing candidate-producer dependencies

Simulation, reconstruction, generation, and other candidate producers depend on adoption targets; production authorities never depend on those producers existing.

## 12.9 Forcing candidate identity matching onto every ingestion route

Camera-only or other domain-specific candidate adoption must not be blocked by object identity matching that is irrelevant to the chosen domain.

## 12.10 Over-gating Performance on universal rigging — or under-gating lip sync on arbitrary audio

The first body/facial Performance Revision requires one exact immutable representation sufficient for its declared workflow, not a completed universal character-animation system. Conversely, dialogue-bound facial performance must not be under-specified as `wav → lip-sync model → video`: G8 must close Dialogue Line, Vocal Performance, exact timebase, derived-alignment, synchronization, and historical-capture semantics before the first lip-sync milestone plan freezes.

## 12.11 Conflating Take approval with persistent consequence or reusable promotion

`RV-01` and `RV-02` remain explicit separate adoption actions. Generated pixels do not author upstream truth automatically.

---

## 12.12 Treating a correction prompt as the production contract

`DX-01` must compile authoritative change scope plus preservation requirements. A text instruction by itself cannot define what is allowed to change or what must remain fixed.

## 12.13 Regenerating accepted work by default

When a bounded correction path can preserve accepted camera/performance/staging/identity more reliably or cheaply, the system should be able to realize the delta rather than requiring a whole-Shot regeneration. This is an execution choice, never an authority change.

## 12.14 Calling a successful operation a passed production verdict

Process completion and domain verdict remain separate. `UNKNOWN`, `NOT_MEASURABLE`, and `REQUIRES_REVIEW` must not collapse into success.

## 12.15 Letting live discovery reinterpret history

Capability/environment discovery is mutable evidence. Readiness/history must depend on a captured/versioned snapshot or contract, not on whatever the environment reports today.

## 12.16 Treating qualification as a global asset flag

A global `locked`/`qualified` flag destroys realization-profile and protocol scope. Qualification must retain the exact revision/profile/protocol/evidence tuple and may diverge across profiles.

## 12.17 Treating attached references as universal authority

Reference media must carry explicit property scope when production-significant. The renderer is not allowed to infer which reference owns which property and then silently promote that inference into production truth.

---


## 12.18 Treating “lossless” as one undifferentiated guarantee

Media preservation must disclose whether the claim is byte-exact, stream-exact, decoded-essence-exact, boundary re-encode, or full re-encode. None of those claims proves that the correct Take/interval or production property was selected.

## 12.19 Letting proxies or executor syntax become editorial authority

A playback proxy may disappear without changing edit meaning, and FFmpeg/NLE/interchange artifacts may change when the executor changes. If either becomes the only durable definition of the edit, the authority direction has inverted.

## 12.20 Scheduling editorial implementation before G12 closes

The v1.6 branch remains intentionally a design boundary, not a milestone. Do not freeze timeline/edit schemas opportunistically inside correction, Sound Post, Performance, or delivery work.

