# 15. Summary

The revised dependency model can be reduced to six production rules:

```text
1. Publish a minimal immutable reusable production revision without first
   overbuilding a generalized representation system.

2. Assemble revisions into compositions whose addressable occurrences have
   durable identity, explicit edit scope, and identity survival across publication.

3. Join those occurrences to existing world-state/spatial authority and capture
   the exact reusable world into immutable historical Shot state.

4. Keep observation-contract design separate from proof that the new reusable
   world actually reaches execution; only the latter closes SHOOT THE WORLD.

5. Let independent branches remain independent: entity-bound intra-Shot events,
   basic QC, camera-only ingestion, performance identity, and relationships do not
   need to wait for the full reusable-world spine when their own authority contracts
   are already satisfied.

6. Keep future editorial decisions downstream of explicit Take select and upstream of
   conform execution: exact sources are immutable, proxies are replaceable, preservation
   classes are explicit, and executor syntax never becomes the edit.
```

The roadmap can now choose implementation order without rediscovering these dependencies inside milestone plans.

Targeted correction remains a downstream option once preservation semantics exist. The new editorial/conform branch is likewise future downstream work and is not a prerequisite for the persistent reusable-world loop or the current Performance program.
